.UPDATE...
Issued at 821 AM PDT Thu Oct 15 2026

No update to the forecast necessary this morning. A Fire Weather
Watch was issued overnight for the North Bay interior mountains
where very dry and windy conditions tonight through Friday morning
will promote rapid spread of any fire ignitions. Winds at the
highest spots are already sustained at 30+ MPH with little to no
overnight relative humidity recovery last night. RH values this
morning are generally in the 20-30% range, and expected to be in the
teens by later today. The decision on whether to upgrade to a Red
Flag Warning will be made this afternoon with the scheduled forecast
update. There are pockets of moderate HeatRisk this afternoon with
the warming temperatures, mainly in the North Bay and East Bay. More
widespread HeatRisk is in store for Friday, including many coastal
areas as offshore flow continues to work against the marine layer.

